    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n25737" root="ضرح" body-key="D">
    
      8 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اضطرحوا فُلَانًا</span></b>  <i>They cast such a one aside:</i>
(O, * L, TA: [see also 1, first sentence:]) the
vulgar say <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اِطَّرَحُوا</span>, thinking it to be from <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الطَّرْحُ</span>,
whereas it is from <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الضَّرْحُ</span>: or, accord. to Az, it
may be that, in <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اطّرحوا</span>, the <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ت</span> of the measure
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اِفْتَعَلَ</span> is changed into <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ط</span>, and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ض</span> incorporated
into it. (L, TA.)

